Changelog: 17-10-2026 10:54:05

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/consoles (was apps/console-link) and its package is consoles_link
(was bc250_console_link): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and a package
without the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the portal, its chapter of
the wiki (apps/consoles/), its installer test and its release tags: consoles-v<x.y.z> from the next release on,
which is also what the app's update check looks for and what the release workflow builds the native wheel for.
The installed app keeps its name, its launcher bc250-console-link, its environment, its settings, its consoles,
its history and its statistics files, and the native core keeps its own name (bc250_console_link_core: the wheel
in the app's environment, which the Dependency Checker asks for FFmpeg); the portal moves its record of the
installed copy to the new key. The development page on the stream's threads keeps its name.

