Changelog: 13-10-2026 13:19:28

Fix, second part (owner's board, 13-10-2026: still sound but no picture from the shortcut): Steam also preloads its overlay, gameoverlayrenderer.so, into a non-Steam game, and it breaks the app's OpenGL; the shortcut's LD_LIBRARY_PATH was empty, so the first part did not apply. Reproduced with the running shortcut's own environment: no OpenGL with the overlay, OpenGL without it. steam_env.py restarts the app without the overlay as well (the rest of LD_PRELOAD kept, and a library path of the user's own); Steam's overlay is then not over the stream on the desktop. Tests: the overlay left, the rest kept.

Fix (owner's board, 13-10-2026: the Steam shortcut streamed sound but no picture; the log said "qt.qpa.wayland: EGL not available" and "QOpenGLWidget: Failed to create context", and Python crashed now and then): Steam starts its programs with its own runtime in LD_LIBRARY_PATH, /usr/lib64 included, so the app's Qt (PyQt6's) mixed with the system's Qt libraries. steam_env.py, run before Qt loads: started with Steam's libraries, the app starts itself again without them (once, marked); in Game Mode (gamescope) it uses X11 unless QT_QPA_PLATFORM is set. Reproduced on the board with Steam's environment (Qt does not even load) and checked: without the path OpenGL works, under Wayland and X11. The shortcut's pictures: the app's own from images/steam/ (portrait.png, wide.png, hero.png, logo.png) where there is one, the console's name and model written over the portrait and the wide one on a dark band (owner); the banner as it is (Steam lays the logo image, the console's name, over it); the drawn banner and logo at Steam's largest sizes (3840 × 1240, 1280 × 720). Tests: leaving Steam's libraries once, X11 in Game Mode, the own pictures.

Changelog: 13-10-2026 12:37:38

Fix (owner's board, 13-10-2026: Add to Game Mode closed Steam, then reported that Steam did not close within 30 seconds, changed nothing and did not start Steam again): the app's own finished steam -shutdown stayed behind as a zombie process named steam, which the check counted as Steam still running. steam_running() now ignores zombies, and the Steam commands the app starts are collected when they end. The PS button setting used the same check. Tests: a zombie named steam, and no zombie left by a command.

